HST Office: pure ladder selection for the Office-style collapse of the Tabbed notebookbar.

- vcl/inc/HstRibbonScaling.hxx (new): given the width of every group in each of its size states
  (large first), an ordered ladder of "group g goes to state s" steps and the available width,
  it picks the state of every group and the groups that move into the overflow popup. Plain
  integer arithmetic without LibreOffice types; nothing includes it yet, the collapse engine
  (HstRibbonTab/HstRibbonGroup) uses it. Deterministic and monotone: steps that do not shrink
  the row are skipped, so the applied steps do not depend on the available width and a wider
  window never shows smaller groups. A row exactly as wide as the space fits. An empty ladder
  means right to left, one state at a time. Pinned groups (the right block) never overflow.
  Unit test: tests/unit/test_ribbon_scaling.py.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/vcl/inc/HstRibbonScaling.hxx
@@ -0,0 +1,153 @@
+/* -*- Mode: C++; tab-width: 4; indent-tabs-mode: nil; c-basic-offset: 4 -*- */
+/*
